## {{ ansible_managed }}
## Homebrew refuses to run itself as root, so casks that ship a signed .pkg
## (e.g. temurin) shell out to a bare `sudo ... /usr/sbin/installer` from
## inside brew itself. That call bypasses Ansible's become/--ask-become-pass
## entirely and otherwise hangs forever waiting on a password nothing
## supplies. Scoped to the one binary that actually needs it - not a general
## NOPASSWD grant.
{{ homebrew_installer_sudoers_user }} ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/installer
